# duplicate-action.tflw — CHECK-ONLY FIXTURE (M86): two `action`s in one file sharing a name —
# demonstrates `tflw check`'s teaching diagnostic (TF035: checker, `checkActionDecls`, tflw
# M60/A2-01). Reported at the *second* declaration, pointing back at the first.
#
# Actions are file-scoped, so the second declaration shadows nothing — the call below is simply
# ambiguous, and the runtime refuses to build the file rather than pick one. Worth catching
# statically: the two bodies here differ, so whichever a silent winner-takes-all rule chose, half
# the suite would be asserting against the other one.
#
# Run explicitly (dot-directory, invalid syntax — see bad-keyword.tflw's header for why):
#   npx tflw check tests/.checkonly/duplicate-action.tflw

action fetch health()
  api GET /health
  expect status equals 200

action fetch health()
  api GET /health
  expect body.status equals "ok"

test "calls an ambiguously-declared action"
  fetch health()
